#: includes/core/class-sstk-posts-app-server.php:279
msgid ""
"Well, this is embarassing.  It looks like this process is taking a very very "
"long time which is unusual. So here are some things you might want to double-"
"check:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/core/class-sstk-posts-app-server.php:281
msgid ""
"1. It is possible that there is a login issue or an api key issue. The two "
"most common issues are incorrectly configured ssh keys and incorrectly "
"configured api keys."
msgstr ""

#: includes/core/class-sstk-posts-app-server.php:282
msgid ""
"2. Some cloud providers such as VULTR and UPCLOUD might require you to "
"whitelist your IP address or explicitly require that you enable use of their "
"API."
msgstr ""

#: includes/core/class-sstk-posts-app-server.php:283
msgid ""
"3. Is WP-CRON running properly? Without it our background processes will not "
"run and this process cannot be completed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/core/class-sstk-posts-app-server.php:284
msgid ""
"4. Verify that ssh port 22 is open on the server on which the Simple Stack "
"site is installed. Many commercial WordPress hosts do not allow direct ssh "
"connections out of their WordPress servers."
msgstr ""

#: includes/core/class-sstk-posts-app-server.php:285
msgid ""
"5. Check to see if there are any messages in your WordPress debug.log file."
msgstr ""

#: includes/core/class-sstk-posts-app-server.php:286
msgid ""
"6. Check the SSH LOG screen for error messages that might provide a clue as "
"to what's going on."
msgstr ""

#: includes/core/class-sstk-posts-app-server.php:288
msgid ""
"You can opt to cancel this process and restart it or you can wait a bit "
"longer to see if it continues normally."
msgstr ""

#: includes/core/class-sstk-posts-app-server.php:290
msgid ""
"If you cancel this process you can delete the server from the server list "
"and then try again."
msgstr ""

